senses.gloss:
(I)--a son of दृषद्वती and उशीनर known for his munificence; परीक्षित् compared to him. Knew the yoga power of Hari;
1: भा. I. १२. २०; II. 7. ४५; Va. ९९. २१-23.
father of वृषादर्भ and three other sons (ten sons-म्। प्।); gave up life in service, and attained per- manent fame.
2: भा. IX. २३. 3-4; VIII. २०. 7; X. ७२. २१; Vi. IV. १८. 9-१०; M. ४८. १९-20.
शिवपुरम् was his capital;
3: Br. III. ७४. २०-23.
engaged in a [page३-418+ २७] sacrifice with Vasumat, अष्टक and Pratardana when his grandfather ययाति fell from heaven;
4: M. ३५. 5; ३८. २२; ४२. २८; ४८. १८.
discoursed with ययाति about other worlds;
5: Ib. ४२. 6-8.
went to heaven in a golden chariot;
6: Ib. ४२. १४, २६.
gifts of, to attain heaven.
7: Ib. ४२. १९.
